From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:08:28 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 09/60] Plutonium: set the DRM device id for a Vulkan device
 shared with ANGLE

VulkanDeviceQueue::InitializeFromANGLE (VulkanFromANGLE) didn't copy
drm_device_id from the physical device info, as Initialize does. Exo's
dmabuf feedback then names no device, and Wayland clients fall back to
software rendering. Needed for linux-chromeos on X11 with ANGLE on Vulkan,
the configuration in which WebGL and canvases work with Vulkan compositing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TNhRAcr4c5t15KWH3mHxTk
---
 gpu/vulkan/vulkan_device_queue.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gpu/vulkan/vulkan_device_queue.cc b/gpu/vulkan/vulkan_device_queue.cc
index a97235c08f..2d9809f413 100644
--- a/gpu/vulkan/vulkan_device_queue.cc
+++ b/gpu/vulkan/vulkan_device_queue.cc
@@ -473,6 +473,10 @@ bool VulkanDeviceQueue::InitializeFromANGLE(bool is_thread_safe) {
   vk_physical_device_properties_ = physical_device_info.properties;
   vk_physical_device_driver_properties_ =
       physical_device_info.driver_properties;
+  // Plutonium: as in Initialize(). Exo's dmabuf feedback names this device;
+  // without it (VulkanFromANGLE) clients aren't told the GPU and fall back
+  // to software rendering.
+  drm_device_id_ = physical_device_info.drm_device_id;
 
   VkDevice vk_device = gl::QueryVkDeviceFromANGLE();
   VkQueue vk_queue = gl::QueryVkQueueFromANGLE();
